From d039ff6179592064d1646c06c85dbabaea90b1f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Wakely <jwakely@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:28:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: Re-enable some pb_ds tests for C++17 and later

I disabled these tests for C++17 in r7-2679-gc42966921a2897 due to
ambiguous string conversions in __gnu_pbds::test::basic_type. I think
those ambiguous conversions were due to LWG 2946, so would have gone
away with r8-3329-g4cf5930fdc5765 (fixing PR libstdc++/79162).

In any case, the tests all compile as C++17 now so let's re-enable them.

libstdc++-v3/ChangeLog:

	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/hash_map_rand.cc: Remove c++17
	target selector.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/hash_set_rand.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/list_update_map_rand.cc:
	Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/list_update_set_rand.cc:
	Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/priority_queue_rand.cc:
	Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/tree_map_rand.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/tree_set_rand.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/trie_map_rand.cc: Likewise.
	* testsuite/ext/pb_ds/regression/trie_set_rand.cc: Likewise.

(cherry picked from commit 3b60e2204e225ea643fe54a999848f99d49a6659)
